{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/810978-atlantean-hate","id":810978,"title":"Atlantean hate??","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-17T22:48:39-08:00","id":810978,"title":"Atlantean hate??","content":"I've noticed there's a whole lot of hate (or at least general distaste) for the Atlantean pantheon, and I'm sort of confused as to why. Is it simply because of the fact that it was published with the mention the developers had no plans for using them (which I can totally understand) or is it actual distaste for the pantheon itself?<br /> <br /> Because in all honesty, I find the pantheon fascinating, albeit pointed, and was able to use it as a building block for our very own self-esteem pantheon. Additionally, I didn't find much wrong with the pantheon or its purview, or at least not a lot more than other pantheons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10163-toomuchjesus","name":"Toomuchjesus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T22:50:00-08:00","id":810979,"title":"","content":"In our very first multiple-story campaign, which mirrored many events of LRtH, my players were brought to the fallen Overworld of the Atlanteans by a demigod, where they encountered a preserved scion of Badarus, who, upon being awakened from cryo, agreed to help them with their quest if they helped him restore Atlantis.<br /> This opened up a story arc for their next adventure. They joined the young man, who was at this point a member of their Band, in finding the cause for the desolation in Atlantis, and beginning to reverse it, all the while encountering clues left behind by Badarus, whose far-reaching and nearly exact foresight allowed him to predict the plot of the quest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10163-toomuchjesus","name":"Toomuchjesus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T06:12:33-08:00","id":811081,"title":"","content":"From what I understand, it's dislike because it isn't based off a real life mythos, much like how the patriotic pantheons introduced in the WWII chapter of Scion Companion are often scorned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T08:14:31-08:00","id":811130,"title":"","content":"I imagine it's the same reason players were disappointed by the addition of Atlanteans as a new Pantheon in the Age Of Mythology expansion pack, as opposed to a faction based on an actual mythos. When a large part of your appeal is Zeus and Thor having a fistfight over thunderclouds, popping in with a wholly invented thunder-deity to act as a third patron lacks the same appeal \u2013 just as a fight between Captain America and Batman isn't going to draw much bigger crowds if you throw in Justice Bob, your new OC, no matter how marvellously he's been conceived.<br /> <br /> That said, in Scion's specific case it probably didn't help that the role of the Atlanteans \u2013 illustrating a Pantheon that had been utterly cast down and forgotten \u2013 could have been filled by other, real-world Pantheons who have been almost or completely lost to us. I imagine the next edition will approach that same idea from a very different angle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/605-revlid","name":"Revlid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar605_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T10:04:40-08:00","id":811177,"title":"","content":"People <i>knew</i> that Scion was a limited-book gameline, that it was only going to get a very few books. So there was a lot of feeling that the space given to the Atlantean and WW2 Pantheons was &quot;wasted&quot; space that <i>should</i> have gone to more real-world Pantheons. In a larger game line, I think that resentment wouldn't have been as strong. But when it's one with a very small number of books, there's a strong feeling that unwanted material is 'stealing' space from more 'deserving' material. <br /> <br /> <br /> Which I actually agree with. Somehow an alternate-history WW2 setting with &quot;gods&quot; made up from newspaper cartoons was cooler than Babylon? Laaaaaame.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T19:02:58-08:00","id":818133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/810978-atlantean-hate?p=811081#post811081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I understand, it's dislike because it isn't based off a real life mythos, much like how the patriotic pantheons introduced in the WWII chapter of Scion Companion are often scorned.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I like the idea of Gods being created through human belief and spirituality. Hell, that is pretty much the entire opening narrative for Scion. The Gods were afraid mortals could alter their existence, so they jumped ship to the Overworld for a few thousand years.<br /> <br /> <br /> It also serves as a basis or guideline for how new / original pantheons can be created. For example, I've heard there is a group out there who actually believes in <i>The Force</i> as a religion. Which means theoretically, you could have a pantheon derived from Star Wars for a sweet cross over. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> The reason I dislike the WW2 pantheons is because of how rushed and tacked on they felt. The allied Pantheon has not one, but three countries / cultures to draw ideas from, and the best they could come up with is 3 figures from each.<br /> <br /> <br /> Br'er Rabbit is supposed to be Coyote, as well, so technically he is based on real world mythology. But it would have been better to have a full pantheon of Native Americans instead of absorbing just one of them into the Yankees.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 01-27-2016, 10:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T01:04:44-08:00","id":818275,"title":"","content":"Human belief and spirituality can <i>affect</i> the Gods of Scion, but cannot create or shape them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T01:10:47-08:00","id":818279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/810978-atlantean-hate?p=818275#post818275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Human belief and spirituality can <i>affect</i> the Gods of Scion, but cannot create or shape them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I thought creating them was the plot behind the Atlanteans returning to power. Their entire civilization was wiped out, but the collective belief of humanity brings them back. Or did I misinterpret that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T01:38:46-08:00","id":818290,"title":"","content":"In this case it's more about reshaping what was already there. They don't get created from nothing with the sole foundation of human belief but rather are resurrected by the fact people start believing in them again. That may sound like a minor difference at first, but if it'd be possible for humanity to create gods from basically nothing, I'd wager that the Titans would've used that against the gods ages ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8325-asmael","name":"Asmael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T05:27:58-08:00","id":818353,"title":"","content":"I share the same feelings as Telgar on this. They used word-count to detail a fictional pantheon when they could have included any number of extremely cool real pantheons. This probably would not have been a big deal in game with a dozen or more books, but the extremely limited number of books means that we were all starved for real pantheons.<br /> <br /> Put another way, this game attracts a lot of mythology fans. Those fans were really eager for some more mythology and were given something that was definitely not mythology. So naturally we were all scratching our heads and wondering what went wrong. It was like tuning into the History channel and seeing a program about alien abductions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1505,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","user":"Charles Red","date":". 01-28-2016, 08:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T10:50:41-08:00","id":818576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/810978-atlantean-hate?p=818279#post818279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I thought creating them was the plot behind the Atlanteans returning to power. Their entire civilization was wiped out, but the collective belief of humanity brings them back. Or did I misinterpret that?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't see how that could be, since literally no one knows of the Atlanteans at all. My understanding is that they were presented as an <i>extinct</i> Pantheon that could be used in historical games, as Titan-corrupted antagonists or under other special circumstances. Which... further added to the insult and hate. They took up word count that <i>could</i> have gone to a real-life Pantheon and they weren't even <b>usable in most games</b>. That was really annoying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T11:12:30-08:00","id":818588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charles Red</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/810978-atlantean-hate?p=818353#post818353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Put another way, this game attracts a lot of mythology fans. Those fans were really eager for some more mythology and were given something that was definitely not mythology. So naturally we were all scratching our heads and wondering what went wrong. It was like tuning into the History channel and seeing a program about alien abductions.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be on H<sub>2</sub>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T11:56:29-08:00","id":818614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charles Red</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/810978-atlantean-hate?p=818353#post818353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Put another way, this game attracts a lot of mythology fans. Those fans were really eager for some more mythology and were given something that was definitely not mythology. So naturally we were all scratching our heads and wondering what went wrong. It was like tuning into the History channel and seeing a program about alien abductions.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are parts of the Atlanteans I like, but even out of extinct pantheons, there are better ones to choose from. I don't think they'll be returning until we're very deep into 2e, if at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T12:01:00-08:00","id":818617,"title":"","content":"Alternately, if I were to make a guide on the blog or a little PDF product on creating your own fictional pantheon rather than adapting an already extant historical culture, then the Atlanteans would be a prime target. <b>Scion 2e</b>'s able to handle fictional pantheons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T12:58:42-08:00","id":818660,"title":"","content":"There are better fictional pantheons out there than the Atlanteans. Many of them on expired copyrights even or with holders willing to work with respectful fans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T23:29:52-08:00","id":819022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/810978-atlantean-hate?p=818660#post818660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are better fictional pantheons out there than the Atlanteans. Many of them on expired copyrights even or with holders willing to work with respectful fans.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wanna play a scion of MANA-YOOD-SUSHAI.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T00:10:42-08:00","id":819031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/810978-atlantean-hate?p=819022#post819022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wanna play a scion of MANA-YOOD-SUSHAI.</div> </div> </div> </div>...So you can sleep all the time and make people worry about how cranky you'll be when you wake up?<br /> <br /> ...Would play also. *nods*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T05:34:25-08:00","id":819142,"title":"","content":"I personally would have found the American Pantheon more interested if it was a Pantheon of ascended Scions from various other places that got together with a mix of some older types taking on new faces rather than &quot;Well they just exist&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T08:43:00-08:00","id":819283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/810978-atlantean-hate?p=819142#post819142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally would have found the American Pantheon more interested if it was a Pantheon of ascended Scions from various other places that got together with a mix of some older types taking on new faces rather than &quot;Well they just exist&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well most of those in the pantheon actually are from popular folk lore / mythology. Except for Uncle Sam who's just a national icon that didn't really do anything besides show up on posters.<br /> <br /> Johnny Appleseed, Pecos Bill and Paul Bunyan, however, are definitely Scion material. though you're right, it would be nice to know where they came from. Only three of the WW2 deities are stated to be former Scions, and they're all from Athena...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T09:41:08-08:00","id":819331,"title":"","content":"its just &quot;Special snowflake&quot; Hate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T10:22:29-08:00","id":819354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/810978-atlantean-hate?p=819331#post819331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">its just &quot;Special snowflake&quot; Hate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so. Particularly when the dominant thread of people's explanation is &quot;it took up space that could have been used to detail another ACTUAL pantheon based on another ACTUAL mythology&quot;. <br /> <br /> There is nothing particularly &quot;special snowflake&quot; about the Atlantean pantheon beyond the fact the authors made them up out of whole cloth. Scire fits right in to the general slop of PSPs. The deities didn't have any particular fancy side stuff that made them different from the already detailed gods. (No, &quot;Atlantean gods get the PSPs of other pantheons&quot; or &quot;Atlantean gods get 12 abilities&quot; or the like). There was some truncation in the conceptualizations of their Underworld and Overworld, admittedly, but, overall, those fit in with the core themes of the pantheon and it would be very easy to see similar ideas being applied to other pantheons with mythologies that don't fit so comfortably into the whole tripartate conceptualization. <br /> <br /> They aren't even really the only &quot;made up&quot; pantheon, as the Allied pantheons are effectively &quot;made up&quot; particularly with regard to the idea of them being any sort of group. There's not much more than individual mythologies (if that). No actual &quot;pantheon&quot; mythology. There aren't many well known stories of Uncle Sam going out to get Paul Bunyan to fell a big tree that was killing all the crops in Virginia because it cast too much shade or Betsy Ross calling on Pecos Bill to go out and harvest some strange desert plant for a very special flag she wanted to sew... <br /> <br /> The Nemetondevos are effectively another &quot;made up&quot; pantheon, since there is next to nothing in the way of individual mythologies much less anything that identifies them as a pantheon proper (except of course that they were, there's just no evidence of it). Not many people have the same feelings about the Gallic deities as the hate on for the Atlantean. Aside from the largely fictional nature of the end product, at least it's about actual gods some people worshiped at some point in time. (And really, there's not any other way to create a &quot;lost&quot; pantheon than making it up almost entirely.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T05:10:59-08:00","id":819768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/810978-atlantean-hate?p=819283#post819283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Well most of those in the pantheon actually are from popular folk lore / mythology. Except for Uncle Sam who's just a national icon that didn't really do anything besides show up on posters.<br /> <br /> Johnny Appleseed, Pecos Bill and Paul Bunyan, however, are definitely Scion material. though you're right, it would be nice to know where they came from. Only three of the WW2 deities are stated to be former Scions, and they're all from Athena...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think there could have been some mileage out of &quot;Uncle Sam is a new face for God x..&quot; like Aries and Mars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T10:41:26-08:00","id":819874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/810978-atlantean-hate?p=811177#post811177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People <i>knew</i> that Scion was a limited-book gameline, that it was only going to get a very few books. So there was a lot of feeling that the space given to the Atlantean and WW2 Pantheons was &quot;wasted&quot; space that <i>should</i> have gone to more real-world Pantheons. In a larger game line, I think that resentment wouldn't have been as strong. But when it's one with a very small number of books, there's a strong feeling that unwanted material is 'stealing' space from more 'deserving' material.<br /> <br /> <br /> Which I actually agree with. Somehow an alternate-history WW2 setting with &quot;gods&quot; made up from newspaper cartoons was cooler than Babylon? Laaaaaame.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I agree with this 100% I personally liked the Atlantean Pantheon, not so much the WW2 Pantheon because at least the Atlanteans, while were based on some fictional work were<br /> A) Based on some VERY OLD fictional work, from someone who came from the era in which the Dodeketheon were still worshiped [if I remember right]<br /> B) Still, despite being fictional, were done well enough in said fictional world that they regularly get used as though the location was in fact a real place, and are done well enough that it still causes people to, on occasion go &quot;What if.....&quot; <br /> <br /> But yes, if your going to have a limited run book, don't waste word count on a pantheon you already say &quot;Hey this Pantheon is Dead, we're not using it&quot;, and focus on one of the many and very interesting real world pantheons that had actual worshipers as the mentioned Babylon, or the Polynesian gods [Who doesn't want to play a Samoan Warrior?], or hell, even dip into the Native American Pantheons as they used Coyote in one of their stories already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'll be your Huckleberry","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2397-the-dude","name":"The Dude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T12:46:58-08:00","id":819924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Dude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/810978-atlantean-hate?p=819874#post819874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...at least the Atlanteans, while were based on some fictional work were<br /> A) Based on some VERY OLD fictional work, from someone who came from the era in which the Dodeketheon were still worshiped [if I remember right]<br /> B) Still, despite being fictional, were done well enough in said fictional world that they regularly get used as though the location was in fact a real place, and are done well enough that it still causes people to, on occasion go &quot;What if.....&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>A) The story of <i>Atlantis</i> is fictional work, but in that original story, the people of Atlantis worshipped the Greek Gods, too. They were ruled by sons of Poseidon, in fact. They did not have their own culture or Gods. They were Greek, since the person telling the story was Greek and was using Atlantis as an allegory to explain things to a Greek audience.<br /> <br /> B) ...eehhhh. Mostly that only started during the era of Spiritualism, so it's a fairly recent thing. And that's no more equivalent to historical validity than people looking for mole people at the center of the Earth.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T08:29:01-08:00","id":820350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/810978-atlantean-hate?p=818660#post818660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are better fictional pantheons out there than the Atlanteans. Many of them on expired copyrights even or with holders willing to work with respectful fans.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm aware. It's something we've talked about for 2e, given that it's no longer a limited line. Stretch goal pantheons may or may not include fictional pantheons, simply because I'm not liable to use a fictional pantheon in a core book.<br /> <br /> However, the Atlanteans have a distinct advantage, in that they're wholly fictional - and if we're talking about PCs creating their own pantheon, they remain a good example. By Plato's account, Atlas and his family are assuredly Scions, and might've ascended to Godhood. Due to the way Apotheosis and pantheon creation works in 2e, Atlantis is a good sample choice for other &quot;what if&quot; reasons.<br /> <br /> In <b>Scion 2e </b>canon, though, Atlantis is a locked-off Terra Incognita. Getting there via ritual or magics will probably get you to a spot that looks like a much bigger version of the island in <i>Tomb Raider</i>, except with lots of Grecian ruins instead of Japanese ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T09:08:38-08:00","id":820363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/810978-atlantean-hate?p=819331#post819331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">its just &quot;Special snowflake&quot; Hate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, part of the problem with Scion is that it should have been 'Special Snowflake: the game' (or Snowflake: the Special if you want to go all WoD), but it doesn't quite fit that. Scion should be essentially Heracles teaming up with Cuchullian and going to beat up Surtur because he was dumping his rubbish in the park/burning down the Gerkin or something. Which is not to say that I dislike Scion, heck I desperate wish 2e didn't have 4 corebooks so I could afford all of it, but it could have really done that 'everybody is a special snowflake thing'.<br /> <br /> Part of the reason I dislike the Atlantean, Allied, and especially American pantheons is because they take things I couldn't care about (except Robin Hood, who shouldn't be a god but rather an example of a legendary but still mortal person IMO) and turn them into specialer snowflake. I can stomach the Atlanteans, because I can at least use them for story seeds, and really should buy the 1e Demigod and God sometime so I can get more information on them and demigod level play (I'll leave out the horrible 'add this template' part and just have the PCs transition to Demigod with their current stats, and god level play just doesn't interest me), but the Allied and American pantheons make me annoyed at the lack of a Caanite Pantheon, a Persian Pantheon, or any other cool real world pantheons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T09:25:36-08:00","id":820377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/810978-atlantean-hate?p=820363#post820363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...a Persian Pantheon...</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel the need to point out that there's in fact an official supplement about the Persian Gods. You might have missed because it's standalone and easy to overlook.<br /> <br /> Here: <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/81259/Yazata-The-Persian-Gods\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/...e-Persian-Gods</a><br /> <br /> Ok, I'll get back into the shadows.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T09:30:37-08:00","id":820381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/810978-atlantean-hate?p=820377#post820377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel the need to point out that there's in fact an official supplement about the Persian Gods. You might have missed because it's standalone and easy to overlook.<br /> <br /> Here: <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/81259/Yazata-The-Persian-Gods\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/...e-Persian-Gods</a><br /> <br /> Ok, I'll get back into the shadows.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, okay, I take back the Persian one and replace it with another real-world Pantheon that's cool but was left out. The real point was that there are real, extremely cool Pantheons that they could have given us instead of the Allied/Yankee Pantheons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T09:36:08-08:00","id":820385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/810978-atlantean-hate?p=820381#post820381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Huh, okay, I take back the Persian one and replace it with another real-world Pantheon that's cool but was left out. The real point was that there are real, extremely cool Pantheons that they could have given us instead of the Allied/Yankee Pantheons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, I was not trying to undermine your reasoning. Just saying that, aside from the discussion we're having here, if you were looking for a Persian Pantheon there's a supplement where you can find it.<br /> <br /> A little bit of helpful thread derail, don't mind me. I'm reading this topic with interest but I don't have anything to add to the discussion","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T00:25:57-08:00","id":825302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/810978-atlantean-hate?p=819924#post819924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A) The story of <i>Atlantis</i> is fictional work, but in that original story, the people of Atlantis worshipped the Greek Gods, too. They were ruled by sons of Poseidon, in fact. They did not have their own culture or Gods. They were Greek, since the person telling the story was Greek and was using Atlantis as an allegory to explain things to a Greek audience.<br /> <br /> B) ...eehhhh. Mostly that only started during the era of Spiritualism, so it's a fairly recent thing. And that's no more equivalent to historical validity than people looking for mole people at the center of the Earth.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I recently re-read something about them. Plato actually used them as a throw away name for a group in one of his stories. They were meant to be an &quot;other&quot; country, and their sinking after their failing to conqure Athens, was meant as a story to show Hubaris in action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'll be your Huckleberry","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2397-the-dude","name":"The Dude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T09:49:59-08:00","id":825450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Dude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/810978-atlantean-hate?p=825302#post825302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I recently re-read something about them. Plato actually used them as a throw away name for a group in one of his stories. They were meant to be an &quot;other&quot; country, and their sinking after their failing to conqure Athens, was meant as a story to show Hubaris in action.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's pretty certain it wasn't purely meant as fiction, more as a historical allegory. Meaning it was based on what the Athenians thought of their own very distant quasi-pre-legendary-semi-mythic history. Partially via third party source material (in this case the Egyptians). But there are quite a few parallels between what the Athenians knew/thought they knew about the distant past to sorta pin the &quot;Atlanteans&quot; on the later Minoans. Vide the mythology of Minoan/Athenian antipathy in the Theseus stories, the fact the civilization was devastated by a natural disaster of extreme proportions, etc. etc. It may be wishful thinking by the relevant modern folks, on the order of a conspiracy of sorts, but supported enough to argue about (like the Trojan War). <br /> <br /> If you buy it (and a lot of very knowledgeable people do), then the Atlanteans/Minoans weren't even Greeks per se in the sense of worhshipping the Olympians/Theoi. They predated even the earliest iteration of all that with what we know from the Mycenaeans (who, BTW, had a HUGE influence on the Theoi, if the court of Zeus is anything, it's a divine interpolation of the court of a Mycenaen city state, with a king (wanax) aka Zeus, etc.) So they would have had yet another mythology of their own, but it certainly wouldn't have looked anything like the crap in Demigod. It could have come across like the Nemetondevos or something. If you are able to dig hard enough, there are definitely scholars who have spent oodles of time teasing out the Minoan bits from Classical Greek Mythology (want to see Hyacinth as an actual full-fledged god instead of another object lesson who got &quot;flowered&quot;?) and from the archaeological remains. Meaning, another example of the &quot;what in the Hells do we do with 'dead pantheons'?&quot; question.<br /> <br /> For the sake of simplicity, I would just have let Atlantis be a Terra Incognita for the Dodekatheon/Theoi in some way. Then you can keep pretty much keep Plato's story intact and use it in fun ways. For example, why not go for some version of the Aquaman version and have the aquatic kingdom? I mean, if the rulers were descended from Poseidon, maybe he did the usual &quot;listen to the lamentations of his offspring&quot; and did some transmorgrification and saved some Atlanteans. Though he would probably have turned them into pretty seaweed or some interesting fish if he was following the usual precedents. But you get the idea, there are a LOT of ways to update Atlantis as a Terra Incognita and not have it stolen right out from under the feet of the relevant group. <br /> <br /> It just seems downright un-Scion-like to take such an obvious link-in with Greek mythology and plaster over it with later Neo-Theosophist garbage, combined with some outright idea poaching from more modern writers and come up with the Antarctic Atlantis and its pantheon. I think there would have been a lot less resistance if they had just picked some other mythical/legendary name with a different amount of freight to it and used that instead. There might have been less outcry if it had been Thule or Mu (though, again, many of those options are effectively share the same problems, they just don't have the familiarlity factor).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}